So the original behavior is: while dragging, the moment the pointer crosses the midpoint of some LI, the dragging item lands in that LI's slot (before or after). That's the classic behavior, and it works correctly.

My pointer-events implementation instead iterates over all siblings on every move event and applies its own (buggy, swapped) conditions. The correct equivalent of the original's "one insertion per event relative to the hovered LI" under pointer events is: find the LI whose vertical band the pointer is in (or just use the same midpoint rule for each sibling — but with the correct conditional logic).

The cleanest fix to match the original behavior exactly: for each sibling (in DOM order), insert before if the pointer is above that sibling's midpoint, otherwise after — i.e., a literal port of the original's formula (my earlier trace showed that naively applying this to all siblings in one pass doesn't converge correctly). Instead, do the original thing: find the hovered LI (the one under the pointer: pointer is within li's bounds, or the nearest one), and insert before/after it.

But the pointer might be outside all LIs (above the first, below the last). Original semantics: if the pointer is above li's midpoint → before li. A robust single-pass version that reproduces the same result in all positions:

For each sibling li (in DOM order, excluding the one being dragged):
  before = e.clientY < li.top + li.height/2
  if (before) { /* pointer is above li's midpoint */ 
    if dragging is currently after li → move dragging to immediately before li
  } else {
    if dragging is currently before li → move dragging to immediately after li
  }

This is exactly the original's two-branch logic, just applied deterministically for every sibling:

```js
var sibs = ...;
for each sib:
  var r = sib.getBoundingClientRect();
  var before = e.clientY - r.top < r.height / 2;
  var liAfterSib = dragging.compareDocumentPosition(sib) & 2; // FOLLOWING means sib follows li; so li is after sib ⇔ sib precedes li ⇔ NOT(sib follows li)
```

Note: li.compareDocumentPosition(sib) & FOLLOWING (4) ⇔ sib is after li ⇔ li is before sib.
So "li is after sib" = NOT that bit.

Original: before && liAfterSib → insertBefore(li, sib);  !before && liBeforeSib → insertAfter.

So:

```js
for (var i = 0; i < sibs.length; i++) {
  var sib = sibs[i];
  var r = sib.getBoundingClientRect();
  var before = (e.clientY - r.top) < r.height / 2;
  var liAfterSib = !(drag.li.compareDocumentPosition(sib) & Node.DOCUMENT_POSITION_FOLLOWING);
  if (before && liAfterSib) drag.list.insertBefore(drag.li, sib);
  else if (!before && !liAfterSib) drag.list.insertBefore(drag.li, sib.nextSibling);
}
```

